==German==

===Etymology===
Backformation from the {{etyl|nl|de}} plural {{m|nl|Boeren}} from {{m|nl|Boer}}. The word originally means “farmer” in Dutch but also in several German dialects, which is probably why the form ''Bur'' was avoided in German. (The word {{m|de|Bauer}}, and even more ''Bur'' as a dialectal form, may have the pejorative implication of an illiterate person. Compare {{cog|en|boor}}.)

